{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/82360-sources-for-new-solars-help","id":82360,"title":"Sources for New Solars [Help!]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-01T15:28:36-08:00","id":82360,"title":"Sources for New Solars [Help!]","content":"Alright, I'm going to be STing a game pretty soon for all new players. We've got three Solars as well as a Fiend using Loom-Snarling Deception to <i>pretend</i> to be a Solar.<br /> <br /> Now, I know at least one of the guys gets decision paralysis easily, so I'm going to pick out a few sources and have those be the &quot;default&quot; Solar charmset. I was thinking Core, Ink Monkies, Ever-Cascading Torrent of Glory, and Hundredfold Facets of Enlightenment as sources.<br /> <br /> I'll also be using the Book of the Emerald Circle, Kyeudo's Warstrider Fix, Masters of Jade (for CRM; more as an under-the-hood thing until the players decide to TAKE OVER THE WORLD!), and the Armorium. I mean, Infernals are easy since all their charms are in, like, two books, so...<br /> <br /> Are the above good sources for newer players? I'll be making hand-outs for each ability that people can glance on through when picking their Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-01T19:49:05-08:00","id":82462,"title":"","content":"For Solars, I'd stick with the Core + Scroll of Errata, with a liberal picking of stuff from the Ink Monkeys (the number of melee charms available from that are insane, so choose sparingly). I would also question the use of the Armorium and Hundredfold Facets of Enlightenment--some of the stuff in there are of questionable balance, IIRC.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/339-armstrong-thunderbolt","name":"Armstrong Thunderbolt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar339_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T02:04:16-08:00","id":82563,"title":"","content":"I'd agree with the above. For new players, the Core plus errata is enough. Once they've got characters under their belt, they can move on to the Ink Monkey's stuff, and then fan things if you want. It's how we did it back in the early days of 2nd ed, before all these newfangled &quot;extra books&quot; and &quot;fanworks&quot; came out. Damn kids, they've got it so good...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-02T08:07:43-08:00","id":82634,"title":"","content":"I agree with the others. We have relatively experienced players and allow Charms from the hardback books only by default, plus the errata document because we are playing in 2.5. So for Solars, that's the core book, Abyssal book, Infernals book, and Scroll of Errata.<br /> <br /> Players can learn Ink Monkey, Glories of the Most High, Scroll of the Monk, etc. Charms with permission and the ST reserves the right to house rule those Charms basically on the spot (where you can change your mind and not buy it if you don't like the ruling).<br /> <br /> Mileage may vary, but we've also reverted all Charms that give Overdrive or Attunement motes back to their original versions, where possible. Also, all Exalted have the First, Second, and Third Excellency available without XP cost everywhere where they meet the Minimums and Prerequisites. You still have to buy the other General Charms, but it has been a lot of fun and we like it.<br /> <br /> The ST also chose to eliminate the Dawn keyword for reasons I won't go into, which only affects me and has been fine.<br /> <br /> Taking it a step further, a previous ST did free Ox-Body Technique per dot of Essence, as long as you met the trait Minimums, which we also enjoyed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/994-heroicantagonist","name":"heroicantagonist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar994_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T23:25:07-08:00","id":85126,"title":"","content":"As a general rule, the fewer complications your new players have to deal with, the less trouble they'll have getting into the game. And getting anywhere outside of the Core + Errata is likely to get very complicated, especially once you get into the Ink Monkeys War Charms, the shrikes, and other mechanical weirdness that you should only really introduce one they're comfortable with the base system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;We do not quit playing because we grow old, we grow old because we quit playing.&quot; - Oliver Wendell Holmes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/283-mrinsecure","name":"MrInsecure","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"385"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}